column3:
"To explore, learn, capture and communicate the 200 year heritage of The Old Market in Hove (and wider Brunswick Town Development). This anniversary falls in 2025, alongside a significant development for the Old Market (becoming a registered charity) and represents a significant milestone for the organisation to reflect on it's past, and re/connect with local communities, audiences, artists and stakeholders.

We will:

- work with a local historian to better understand the history of our building and its place in the local community;
- work with local street artists to communicate the changing uses of the building through murals co-created with local groups (with associated information pannels);
-   Capture our local communities oral histories of the space throughout the years to create a digital sound installation around the building;
- Host a 'birthday' community event with our direct neighbours to celebrate the 200th birthday of The Old Market."

"The North Craven Building Preservation Trust is at a critical point, changing from an entirely volunteer-run organisation to one employing professional staff to manage a portfolio of listed buildings requiring renovation and re-use. To ensure organisational resilience, we need to raise our public profile, consult our communities and address weaknesses in our current administrative processes. 
We plan to:
strengthen our IT capacity and skills;
replace outdated hardware and implement software to support file-sharing for communication and planning and to provide data security for business-critical information;
reduce our carbon footprint by minimising data duplication and optimising digital storage and efficient file-sharing;
develop a new website to promote our building preservation activity;
strengthen our use of digital to support income generation;
commission community consultation to inform our 10-year strategic vision;
train our volunteers to develop robust digital skills, in particular to provide stability in periods when we have no paid project staff."
